\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 What Is React Router DOM?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 React Router DOM
\f1\b0  is a library that enables 
\f2\b client-side routing
\f1\b0  in React applications.\
React applications are typically built as 
\f2\b Single Page Applications (SPA)
\f1\b0 . In a traditional website, when you click a link:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The browser sends a request to the server\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The entire page reloads\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 With React Router DOM:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The page does NOT reload\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The URL changes\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Only the relevant component re-renders\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Routing is handled entirely in the browser using JavaScript.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

